# One line. Run from the repo root by
# `orgasmic verify TASK-FZB6T --artifact verify/TASK-FZB6T.1`.
#
# The two "stale identity mistaken for live identity" rules, one test each:
#
# 1. a pruned worktree whose path is later reused by an unrelated checkout must
#    stay tombstoned — the run is dead and no directory that merely answers to
#    the same name may make it an attach candidate again;
# 2. a snapshot entry is admitted through session-directory authority and
#    current file identity, so a wrong parent, a nested path, a `..` traversal,
#    a missing file, a non-session extension, a symlink, and a stale fingerprint
#    are each refused rather than loaded as a run record;
# 3. and — separately, which is the point (TASK-FZB6T.3 finding 5) — an entry
#    whose SEMANTIC claims its own retained envelopes do not reproduce is
#    refused. This used to be the tail of test 2, so under the injection the
#    first path case panicked and these assertions were never reached: the
#    replay passed while proving the wrong red.
env -u ORGASMIC_RUN_ID -u ORGASMIC_HOME cargo test -p orgasmic-daemon --lib -- a_recreated_worktree_at_the_same_path_does_not_revive_a_tombstone semantically_corrupt_snapshot_entries_are_refused a_snapshot_entrys_semantic_claims_must_be_reproduced_by_its_own_envelopes
